  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following reaction\n\\[\n\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{B} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}\n\\]\nThe time taken for \\(\\mathrm{A}\\) to become \\(1 / 4^{\\text {th }}\\) of its initial concentration is twice the time taken to become \\(1 / 2\\) of the same. Also, when the change of concentration of \\(B\\) is plotted against time, the resulting graph gives a straight line with a negative slope and a positive intercept on the concentration axis.\nThe overall order of the reaction is _______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $1^{\\text {st }}$ order reaction\n$75 \\% \\text { life }=2 \\times 50 \\% \\text { life }$<br />So order with respect to A will be first order.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/zYWROYs_DRk3nq1JMNpp9pIsGUKkggtDQbaAOBMPk5g.original.fullsize.png\"><br />So order with respect to B will be zero. Overall order of reaction $=1+0=1$",
    "image": null
  },
